# MainV2's connection controls, ported from MainV2.Designer.cs and MainV2.cs (PLAN.md §13.6 row 80).
#
# The claim: the port box, the baud box and CONNECT sit at the top right of the window
# (MainV2.Designer.cs:176-190, Controls/ConnectionControl.Designer.cs); the port box's list is
# filled when clicked with the machine's serial ports and AUTO, TCP, UDP, UDPCl and WS
# (MainV2.cs:1283-1290, 961-975); choosing TCP dims the baud box (ConnectionControl.cs:24-30);
# CONNECT asks TCP's two questions - "remote host" then "remote Port", each offered from the
# settings or the transport's default (ExtLibs/Comms/CommsTCPSerial.cs:112-125) - and opens the
# link; the button reads DISCONNECT while connected and both boxes go dim (MainV2.cs:2459-2482);
# DISCONNECT closes the link, and a model at rest is not asked about (MainV2.cs:1841-1880,
# 1389-1447). The settings are saved after each (MenuConnect_Click: comport TCP, TCP_host,
# TCP_port), and each question's OK keeps its answer as InputBox keeps every titled answer - the
# transports' OnInputBoxShow is an InputBox.Show (Program.cs:564-566; InputBox.cs:73-84, 178-184).
#
# Divergences, written at their sites in crates/mp-gui/src/main.rs and connect.rs: AUTO's port
# scan (CommsSerialScan) is not ported and is refused on the status line; "Invalid BaudRate" is a
# status line, never a box (the owner's ruling of 2026-09-25).
#
# The application starts with no link: its own settings file, empty, and an empty config.xml, so
# nothing is opened at start-up (the saved link and the settings' comport both would be).
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760. Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/main-connect.gui

env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK
env TMPDIR $WORK
env MP_SETTINGS $WORK/settings.conf
setup mkdir -p "$WORK/MissionPlannerRust" && printf '<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><Config></Config>' > "$WORK/MissionPlannerRust/config.xml"

screen fly
window 1600x1200
settle 4

expect vehicle.connected false
expect link.button CONNECT
expect link.prompt none
expect link.baud 115200
# The boxes at the top right, the button after them.
expect main-port left-of main-baud
expect main-baud left-of main-connect

# `CMB_serialport_Click`: the list, with the five kinds after the machine's ports.
click main-port
settle 1
expect link.ports >= 5
# The five kinds come after the machine's ports; with thirty-odd serial ports the list scrolls.
reveal main-port-list main-port-TCP
click main-port-TCP
settle 1
expect link.port TCP

# `Connect` → `CommsTCPSerial.Open`: the host, then the port, each with its default.
expect config.InputBoxremotehostEnterhostnameipensureremoteendisalreadystarted none
expect config.InputBoxremotePortEnterremoteport none
click main-connect
settle 1
expect link.prompt remote host
key ctrl+u
type 127.0.0.1
key Return
settle 1
expect config.InputBoxremotehostEnterhostnameipensureremoteendisalreadystarted 127.0.0.1
expect link.prompt remote Port
key ctrl+u
type 5760
key Return
settle 8
expect link.prompt none
expect config.InputBoxremotePortEnterremoteport 5760
expect vehicle.connected true
expect link.button DISCONNECT
expect status ~ connected to tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

# `doDisconnect`, without the "still moving" question: SITL sits on the ground.
click main-connect
settle 3
expect vehicle.connected false
expect link.button CONNECT
expect status disconnected
